From 088f1f89965d8398932ca984f080262ff504458c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: christopherrobertbrooks-tech
 <289533927+christopherrobertbrooks-tech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:32:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cuda): keep the DiT residual stream inside float16 range
 (CFG and XL models)

On GPUs without bfloat16 the model runs in float16. With CFG models the gated MLP product of a
decoder layer reaches ~137,000 (2B sft, layers.20) and the XL decoder stream ~1.36 million
(xl-sft, layers.18) -- past float16's 65,504 -- so every latent turns NaN.

Every branch reads the stream through an RMSNorm, which ignores overall scale, and the stream
ends in norm_out. So forward hooks divide what enters the stream (proj_in, self-attention,
cross-attention and MLP outputs) by 64, and the stream-reading norms' epsilon by 64**2: the
decoder output is bit-identical in float32, no weights are modified, and LoRA/LoKr adapters
inside those branches are scaled together with them.

Limits: each branch output must fit float16 before the division (measured <= ~30,000), and the
unscaled stream must stay under 64 * 65,504 (measured 1.36 million). The raw stream returned by
forward(return_hidden_states=...) is scaled too (no in-repo callers).

The fix lives in a new module (fp16_dit_stream.py); the loader calls it only when the model
dtype is float16, and it logs a warning if the decoder is not recognised.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
